[Themes "e5-break"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 d6 4. d4 exd4 5. Nxd4 Bd7 6. Nc3 Nxd4 7. Qxd4 Bxb5 8. Nxb5 Nf6"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "for-us"]
[Opponent "3...d6 4.d4 exd4 5.Nxd4 Bd7 6.Nc3 Nxd4 7.Qxd4 Bxb5 8.Nxb5 Nf6"]
[Start "ruy-lopez-steinitz 8.Nxb5"]

8... Nf6 $2 { Natural, but it leaves c7 and d6 without enough guards. } 9. e5 { Hits the knight on f6, while the knight on b5 eyes c7 and d6. [%cal Ge5f6,Gb5c7] } 9... dxe5 ( 9... Nd7 10. exd6 Bxd6 11. Nxd6+ cxd6 12. Qxg7 { Wins a pawn and wrecks Black's kingside. } ) 10. Qxe5+ { Check, and the queen joins the knight against c7. [%cal Ge5e8,Gb5c7] } 10... Qe7 11. Nxc7+ { A fork of the king and the rook. } 11... Kd7 12. Qxe7+ Bxe7 13. Nxa8 { White has won the rook in the corner. } *
